[1mNAME[0m
     fux-corpus-tables - the engines the corpus is replayed through, in tables

[1mSYNOPSIS[0m
     [1mfux-vt-compare[0m [1mcorpus[0m [[1m--engines[0m [4mlist[24m] [[1m--show[0m] [[4mname[24m...]

[1mDESCRIPTION[0m
     Each recording is replayed through [1mfux-vt[0m and the engines below, and
     their screens are compared after every step.  [4mxterm[24m decides what it can
     tell; the panel decides the rest.

[1mENGINES[0m
     ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
     │[1mEngine[0m      [1mKind[0m         [1mCannot[0m [1mtell[0m                           │
     ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │ghostty     in process   link groups                           │
     │alacritty   in process   blink, 2026, 2048, prompt marks       │
     │libvterm    in process   dim, underline colour, kitty          │
     │avt         in process   underline colour, hidden, keypad      │
     │wezterm     in process   pending wrap, 2026, 2048              │
     │vt100       in process   underline colour, blink, hidden       │
:[K[K     │xterm.js    Node         underline colour, kitty, 2048         │
     │tmux        a server     kitty, 2026, 2048                     │
     │xterm       Xvfb         pending wrap, underline colour, kitty │
     └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

[1mFIELDS[0m
     ┌───────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
     │[1mField[0m  │                        [1mWhat[0m [1mis[0m [1mcompared[0m                        │
     ├───────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │text   │ the whole grapheme cluster of each cell, and its width         │
     ├───────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │style  │ foreground, background and underline colour; bold, dim,        │
     │       │ italic, underline, blink, inverse, hidden and strikeout        │
     ├───────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │link   │ the URI of an OSC 8 hyperlink, and which cells share it        │
     ├───────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │cursor │ its row and column, and whether a wrap is pending              │
     ├───────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │modes  │ DECAWM, DECOM, DECCKM, DECKPAM, bracketed paste, focus         │
     │       │ reports, synchronized output, in-band resize and the kitty     │
     │       │ keyboard flags                                                 │
     └───────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

:[K[K[1mSTATUSES[0m
     • [1mAgree:[0m every step agrees beside xterm and the panel.

     • [1mDiffers:[0m a step differs, for a reason recorded beside it, with the
       command that shows it.

     • [1mNew:[0m a recording with no status, which fails the run until one is
       given.

[1mEXAMPLES[0m
     Replay one recording beside xterm and the panel, and show the screen:

     $ fux-vt/compare/run.sh corpus --show man-tables
     ok       man-tables (9 steps, 6000 bytes)   +xterm +ghostty

     Record it again:

     $ fux-vt/compare/corpus/record.sh man-tables

[1mEXIT[0m [1mSTATUS[0m
     0   every recording expected to agree agrees
     1   one regressed, or has no status
     2   the command line or a recording could not be read
